schema: "0.4"
id: chalkboard-05-flashcard-decks-and-review
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Flashcard Decks & Review — the spaced-repetition
# review surface (SM-2 daily queue) rendered as a chalkboard terminal. HERO screen (rendered
# side-by-side against scholar), so it must carry the chalkboard voice strongly.
# Theme tenets: always-dark forest-green slate board, warm chalk-white hand-lettering, dusty
# colored-chalk accents used categorically (never neon), flat radius-0 board, dashed chalk
# rules + hand-drawn underlines for emphasis (never bold weight).
# Palette: board green #2d4a2d, near-black board #1e2a1e, chalk-white #e8e4d8, sand-chalk
# #c8c0a8, yellow chalk #e8d44c, blue chalk #6cb4dc, rose chalk #e06060, sage chalk #50b878.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a warm,
    always-dark TERMINAL session skinned as a professor's chalkboard — a single focused
    terminal window, not a web page and not a browser. The surface is a spaced-repetition
    review: one flashcard held in focus in the center of a dark forest-green board, quiet deck
    tiles drawn to the side, a few sticks of colored chalk. The card's prompt and answer are
    hand-lettered in a casual print-handwriting face; counts, keys and intervals stay in a
    neat monospace like chalked figures. Emphasis is an underline, never a bold weight. Colored
    chalk is dusty and desaturated, never neon. Flat board, square corners, dashed chalk rules,
    a faint dust of chalk texture. Calm and confirmatory, never gamified.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a focused single-pane TERMINAL session — "The Robot
    Learns" — skinned as a dark green chalkboard, running today's flashcard review. One warm
    forest-green slate board fills the frame like a terminal window. NO browser chrome, NO
    tabs, NO address bar, NO web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT: a centered review card held in focus, a slim left deck rail, and a thin
    progress bar across the top.

    TOP is a slim PROGRESS BAR / milestone tracker for today's queue — a hand-drawn chalk fill
    across a dashed-outline track — with a monospace count beside it, "12 / 40 due".

    A narrow LEFT RAIL carries a SEARCH INPUT BAR drawn as a chalk underline with the written
    label "find a deck" above it, then a short column of DECK SUMMARY TILES. Each tile is a
    dashed chalk-outlined region showing a deck name in display handwriting plus a due-over-total
    count in monospace, "Transformers  8/120", "Elixir/OTP  3/64", "French verbs  15/210"; the
    active deck's title carries a bright yellow-chalk underline.

    The dominant CENTER is a single FLASHCARD held in focus — a hand-drawn chalk-outlined board
    region with generous room. Its FRONT prompt is hand-lettered in warm chalk-white, "What
    does the SM-2 ease factor adjust?"; a dashed chalk rule divides it; then the revealed BACK
    answer in slightly dimmer chalk with one inline monospace term underlined.

    BELOW THE CARD is a GRADE ROW: four chalk-outlined labels "again · hard · good · easy",
    each with a small next-interval hint beneath in monospace, "<10m", "1d", "4d", "9d". The
    four carry tiny dusty chalk dots — rose, amber, sage — used only as small marks and never as
    loud fills; "good" is reinforced with a small underline. A faint monospace status line
    reads "space reveal · 1-4 grade · e export deck".

    PALETTE & TYPE: a deep forest-green slate board as the canvas, one slightly lighter green
    panel for the held card and the deck tiles; lettering in warm dusty chalk-white, secondary
    counts in dimmer sand-chalk. Emphasis and categories in sticks of dusty colored chalk — a
    soft rose-red, a dusty sky-blue, a warm butter-yellow, a sage green — all desaturated like
    real chalk, never bright or neon. Prompts and answers hand-lettered in a casual print
    handwriting face; counts, intervals and keys in a neat monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: flat board with square corners, no rounded cards and no glossy panels;
    separation by dashed chalk rules rather than solid boxes; the held card is a hand-drawn
    chalk outline with slightly uneven edges; a faint even dust of chalk grain and one soft
    eraser smudge.

    MOOD: warm, academic, personal — quiet confirmatory practice, one card at a time, the best
    class you ever took.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, rounded cards, glossy panels, neon or saturated colors, garish gamified colors, dry-erase whiteboard, pure white or light background, bold heavy type"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Flashcard Decks & Review: a top progress bar with due count, a left deck rail with search and deck summary tiles, a centered front/back flashcard, and an again/hard/good/easy grade row — inside one terminal board"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Always-dark forest-green board, warm chalk-white handwriting prompts + mono counts, dusty categorical colored-chalk accents with only tiny reserved grade dots (no neon, not gamified), flat square corners, dashed chalk rules — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Single card held in focus, quiet supporting deck rail, plausible real-product terminal layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "loud gamified or neon colors, or a light/whiteboard background"

tags: [chalkboard, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal, hero]
